<title>USA: St Louis feeder cattle market mixed - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Louis feeder cattle market mixed - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>EAST ST LOUIS, Ill. 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>FEEDER CATTLE AUCTION: 500 head. Compared to last week, feeder steers under 500 lbs were steady, USDA said. Over 500 lbs were weak to $2.00 per cwt lower.</p>
<p>Feeder heifers under 500 lbs were steady. Over 500 lbs $1.00-$3.00 higher. Overall quality was below last week's level. Large buyer attendance.</p>
<p>FEEDER STEERS: Medium and Large Frame 1:</p>
<p>600-700 lbs. 66.00-71.00, crossbreds 71.00-73.00</p>
<p>700-800 lbs. 63.00-67.00</p>
<p>Moderately Fleshy:</p>
<p>500-800 lbs. 61.00-69.00</p>
<p>Fleshy    800-1000 lbs. 57.00-61.00</p>
<p>Large Frame 2 Holsteins: 500-800 lbs. 48.00-53.00.</p>
<p>FEEDER HEIFERS: Medium and Large Frame 1:</p>
<p>600-700 lbs. 63.00-68.00</p>
<p>Moderately Fleshy:</p>
<p>500-700 lbs. 60.00-64.00</p>
<p>700-800 lbs. 53.00-60.00</p>
<p>Receipts 600  Last week  500   Last Year  1,300</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
